                <pb facs="0424" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg414"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Immediate.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Her Majesty’s Treasury to Laird Brothers.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">15, 5862/11.</note>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Chambers,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 2, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> In reply to your letter of the 30th
                    ultimo, representing the danger which the iron-clad vessels now under seizure
                    will incur in consequence of their being removed from your premises, I am
                    commanded by the lords commissioners of her Majesty’s treasury to acquaint you
                    that their lordships, having been in communication with the secretary of state
                    in reference to your letter, have nothing to add to the communication made to
                    you by telegram on the 29th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. A. HAMILTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Birkenhead.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
